{
  "comment": "A request of Claude Code as a card of the feed, and the line each choice writes back (D-294, D-305, D-306). An edit offers 'edits in this session' as its second button. Anything else offers the rule Claude Code suggested, when there is one: for a command the rule has words, for an MCP tool it covers the whole tool (D-307); a command is never answered with the edit mode. A question and a plan have no second button. A refusal without words becomes a plain one. Several picks for one question are joined with a comma, and a question nobody answered is left out. An option may carry a preview, shown under the options of the card (AIKO-327); the card names it only when there is one.",
